---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Business Automations"
	description="Xoaey Digital automates lead follow-up, invoicing, bookings, and reporting for small businesses — fixed price, no jargon."
>
	<section class="xd-hero">
		<div class="xd-container">
			<span class="xd-eyebrow">Service · Business automations</span>
			<h1>
				Stop doing work a <em>workflow</em> should do.
			</h1>
			<p class="xd-lede">
				We connect the tools you already use — CRM, email, calendar,
				accounting — so repetitive work happens automatically and
				accurately, every time.
			</p>
			<div class="xd-btn-row">
				<a href="/contact" class="xd-btn">Get a free automation audit</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="xd-section">
		<div class="xd-container">
			<span class="xd-eyebrow">Symptoms we fix</span>
			<h2>Sound familiar?</h2>
			<ul class="xd-checklist">
				<li>Leads sit in your inbox for days before anyone replies.</li>
				<li>You copy-paste the same details between apps, daily.</li>
				<li>Invoices go out late — and reminders later still.</li>
				<li>Nobody knows the real pipeline number without asking around.</li>
				<li>Evenings disappear into admin instead of the actual business.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="xd-section xd-section-dark">
		<div class="xd-container">
			<span class="xd-eyebrow">What you get</span>
			<h2>Automations that pay for themselves.</h2>
			<div class="xd-grid-2">
				<div class="xd-card">
					<h3>Lead capture &amp; follow-up</h3>
					<p>
						Every enquiry from your site, inbox, and socials lands in
						one pipeline — acknowledged instantly and nurtured with
						timed follow-ups until it converts.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="xd-card">
					<h3>Quotes, invoices &amp; reminders</h3>
					<p>
						Generate quotes in one click, send invoices on schedule,
						and let polite automatic reminders chase late payers —
						with you approving anything sensitive.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="xd-card">
					<h3>Booking &amp; scheduling</h3>
					<p>
						Self-serve calendars with confirmations, rescheduling, and
						reminders. Full diaries, empty inboxes, fewer no-shows.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="xd-card">
					<h3>CRM that runs itself</h3>
					<p>
						Cleanup, enrichment, status updates, and task creation —
						your customer record stays current without manual data
						entry.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="xd-section">
		<div class="xd-container">
			<span class="xd-eyebrow">Process</span>
			<h2>From chaos to autopilot in four steps.</h2>
			<div class="xd-grid-3">
				<div class="xd-card">
					<span class="xd-step-num">1</span>
					<h3>Audit</h3>
					<p>
						Free 30-minute call plus a look at your tools. You get a
						written list of what we'd automate first — yours to keep,
						even if we never work together.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="xd-card">
					<span class="xd-step-num">2</span>
					<h3>Map</h3>
					<p>
						We diagram each workflow and agree what “done” looks like,
						then quote a fixed price. No hourly meters running.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="xd-card">
					<span class="xd-step-num">3</span>
					<h3>Build</h3>
					<p>
						We implement in your accounts (you own everything), test
						with real data, and train your team on video calls you
						can replay.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="xd-section">
		<div class="xd-container">
			<span class="xd-eyebrow">Questions</span>
			<h2>Automation FAQ.</h2>
			<div class="xd-faq">
				<details>
					<summary>Do I need to buy new software?</summary>
					<p>
						Usually not. We start with what you have and only suggest
						new tools when they clearly pay for themselves — and we
						never take commissions on them.
					</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Who owns the automations?</summary>
					<p>
						You do. Everything is built in your accounts, documented in
						plain language, and handed over with training. If we part
						ways, it all keeps running.
					</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>What if something breaks?</summary>
					<p>
						Every workflow includes error alerts — to you and optionally
						to us on a care plan. Most fixes are small config tweaks,
						not rebuilds.
					</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How much does it cost?</summary>
					<p>
						Fixed quotes after the free audit. Small single-workflow
						builds start in the hundreds; full pipeline overhauls are
						scoped individually. You'll know the price before we start.
					</p>
				</details>
			</div>
			<div class="xd-btn-row">
				<a href="/contact" class="xd-btn">Start with a free audit</a>
				<a href="/services/website-design" class="xd-btn-ghost xd-btn">
					See website design
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
